 "desc_header": "IN THIS LESSON",
 "lyrics": "Koala: an adult spends about 19-20 hours/day sitting, sleeping; low energy lifestyle is necessary for an animal that specializes on such a low energy diet; most often described as nocturnal, with some activities during the day; nighttime tree for feeding often not the same tree used in day for resting; eucalyptus branches grow out at sharp angles, which helps koalas wedge themselves in (SDZWA Library fact sheet 'Koala', Behavior & Ecology, ielc.libguides.com/sdzg/factsheets/koala/behavior, read Nov 17 2026).\nLion: may rest up to 20-21 hours per day, on average; peak activity after 5 pm and before 8 am; hunt actively at night; active early and late in the day and at night to avoid the heat of the day; grooming and social licking strengthen the social bonds between pride members; groom and play around dawn and especially in the evening (SDZWA Library fact sheet 'Lion', Behavior & Ecology, ielc.libguides.com/sdzg/factsheets/lions/behavior, read Nov 17 2026).\nPolar bear: sleeping heart rate can fall as low as 8-10 beats/minute; in summer and autumn, bears forced onto land dig sleeping pits and temporary dens (SDZWA Library fact sheet 'Polar Bear', Behavior & Ecology, ielc.libguides.com/sdzg/factsheets/polarbear/behavior, read Nov 17 2026).",
 "script": "Hello, friends! I am Milo the bluebird.\nToday we are learning about sleepy animals!\nWho rests the most? Let's find out!\nThree animal friends will show us. Count them with me. One, two, three!\nStretch and yawn. Let's go!\nWho sits and sleeps in a tree, for most of the day?\nIs it the koala? Or is it the pig?\nIt is the koala!\nHere is the fun fact. A koala sits or sleeps for about twenty hours a day!\nTwenty hours! That is almost the whole day. Shh.\nWhy does a koala rest so much? Hmm.\nIts food is eucalyptus leaves, and they do not give it much energy. So it rests a lot!\nLook at that sleepy koala.\nEucalyptus branches grow out at sharp angles. A koala tucks itself in, nice and snug.\nSnug and safe, high in the tree. Sweet dreams, little koala!\nKoalas often do their eating at night.\nIt may eat in one tree at night, and rest in a different tree in the day!\nSay it with me. A koala rests about twenty hours a day!\nCan you hug a tree like a koala? Hold on tight, and close your eyes.\nNow yawn a big, sleepy koala yawn. Yawn! Shh.\nQuick check! What does a koala do most of the day? Sleeping? Or running?\nSleeping! Shh. Great job!\nWhich big cat may rest for up to twenty hours a day?\nIs it the lion? Or is it the cow?\nIt is the lion!\nHere is the fun fact. A lion may rest for up to twenty hours a day!\nLying in the shade, taking a long, long nap. Yawn! Shh, let it sleep.\nWhen is a lion the busiest? Hmm.\nEarly and late in the day, and at night! That way it stays out of the heat of the day.\nLook at that big, sleepy lion.\nLions do their hunting at night, when it is cooler.\nIn the early morning and in the evening, lions are busy and awake. Up and about!\nLion friends lick each other, to groom. Lick, lick!\nGrooming helps the lions in a family stay close friends. So sweet! Lick, lick, lick!\nSay it with me. A lion rests most of the day!\nCan you stretch like a lion after a nap? Big stretch, and a big yawn!\nNow lick your paw, like a lion grooming. Lick, lick! Nice and clean!\nQuick check! When is a lion busy? At night? Or at lunch time?\nAt night! And early and late in the day. You remembered!\nWhose heart beats very, very slowly when it sleeps?\nIs it the polar bear? Or is it the pig?\nIt is the polar bear!\nHere is the fun fact. When a polar bear sleeps, its heart slows way down!\nPut your hand on your heart. Can you feel it go thump, thump?\nHow slow can a sleeping polar bear's heart go? Hmm.\nAs slow as eight to ten beats in a whole minute! Thump. Thump. Thump.\nLook at that big, white bear.\nIn summer and fall, some polar bears on land dig a sleeping pit.\nDig, dig, dig, then curl up inside. A cozy bed in the ground!\nA polar bear sleeps, and its heart goes slow and steady.\nSlow and steady, while it dreams. Shh! Sleep tight, polar bear.\nSay it with me. A sleeping polar bear has a slow heart!\nCan you dig a sleeping pit like a polar bear? Dig, dig, dig!\nNow curl up, and breathe slow and steady. In, and out.\nQuick check! When a polar bear sleeps, does its heart go slower? Or faster?\nSlower! Thump. Thump. Super thinking!\nWow! We met three sleepy friends. Now it is quiz time!\nGet ready. Think hard!\nWho sits or sleeps about twenty hours a day, in a tree?\nThe koala! Yes!\nWho hunts at night and naps in the day?\nThe lion! That's right!\nWhose heart goes slow when it sleeps?\nThe polar bear! You remembered!\nYou learned so many new things today.\nSnug like a koala. Stretch like a lion. And slow and steady like a polar bear!\nHow do you like to rest?\nThank you for learning with me. Bye-bye, friends! See you next time!",
